    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0177" n="49" xml:id="pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4112Anti-War/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-03T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1928—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>112. Your 122, May 2, 6 p.m. I have heard nothing about either a commission of
                    technical experts or a conference of Foreign Secretaries. If I do, I shall
                    endeavor to discourage their adoption.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
